Why Catalyst has a developer subscription
----------------------------------------

Catalyst is a really cool bunch of stuff that will save you a pile of time
and effort to achieve some of the hardest things required to take your
projects to the next level. It represents a substantial investment of time,
care, and effort from our team. Developer subscriptions help us maintain it,
improve it, and support the community building with it.

Plus, a BenjaVision-Catalyst subscription is only $5 per month, billed
annually at $60 per developer. It gives you access to the BenjaVision-Catalyst
repository. The billing currency is identified at purchase.

We're not trying to get rich from our community. We'll use Catalyst to
build our own products for that. We're aiming for longevity: maintaining
Catalyst for the long term, building our community, and enabling the people
in it to do more.

Our aim is to give developers broad freedom to build with Catalyst, with a
small, predictable contribution from each developer helping sustain its
future. The following terms define those permissions and conditions.

1. Scope and definitions
------------------------

"Software" means the Catalyst software and associated documentation in
this repository supplied under this License, including modified versions
and substantial portions of that material. Material identified as separately
licensed remains governed by its own license.

"Licensor" means the copyright holder granting rights to the Software.
"You" means the individual or organisation exercising those rights.

"Development" means using the Software to develop, modify, integrate,
test, compile, or build a product or a version of a product. It includes
developing modifications to Catalyst itself, bug fixes, security updates,
and rebuilding unchanged source, whether manually or through automation.

"Completed Product" means a product build lawfully created under this
License, including its incorporated Catalyst components. It may be an
executable, library, application bundle, container, or packaged Smalltalk
image. A development or test build may also be a Completed Product.

2. Developer subscriptions and repository access
------------------------------------------------

Every individual developer undertaking Development must have an active
BenjaVision-Catalyst subscription assigned to them while undertaking that
Development. An employer or another organisation may purchase the
subscription on the developer's behalf. A subscription assigned to one
developer does not cover other developers.

An active subscription is a paid subscription within its current annual
term. Paying for one developer does not authorise sharing that developer's
subscription or repository credentials with others.

A subscription provides its assigned developer with access to the
BenjaVision-Catalyst repository for the subscription term. Repository
access ends when the subscription expires. Possession of previously
downloaded source, a fork, or a copy received from someone else does not
remove the subscription requirement for Development.

Automated build systems may perform Development on behalf of subscribed
developers without a separate subscription for each machine or automated
agent. Every individual developer using the Software in that Development
still needs their own active subscription; a single subscribed build
operator does not cover an otherwise unsubscribed development team.

3. Development permissions
--------------------------

Subject to this License and the developer subscription requirement,
permission is granted worldwide and non-exclusively to use, copy, modify,
merge, and build with the Software to create commercial or non-commercial
products, including proprietary products and modified versions of Catalyst.
There is no limit under this License on the number of products or builds a
subscribed developer may create during their active subscription.

You retain ownership of your original work. This License does not require
you to publish your product's source code or contribute modifications back
to Catalyst. You may license your own work under terms of your choice,
provided those terms do not remove the conditions applying to the Software.

4. Perpetual rights for completed products
-----------------------------------------

You and recipients of Completed Products may use, execute, copy, install,
back up, restore, host, deploy, sell, and distribute those Completed Products
indefinitely, without a developer subscription or additional Catalyst
runtime royalties. You may grant recipients those same rights. These
permissions apply to the incorporated Software as needed for those acts.
There is no limit under this License on users, installations, servers, or
copies of a Completed Product.

Expiry or non-renewal of developer subscriptions does not terminate these
permissions for builds lawfully completed before expiry. Historical
contributors do not need to remain subscribed solely because their work
remains in a Completed Product. Customers and operators do not need a
subscription solely to use, host, or distribute a Completed Product.

Copying or deploying an existing build is not Development. Ordinary runtime
execution, including JIT compilation or runtime compilation needed to
execute that existing product, is also permitted without a subscription.
These runtime permissions do not authorise using a Completed Product as a
development tool to undertake Development without the required subscriptions.

Further Development, including a new build of unchanged source or a modified
Smalltalk image, requires active subscriptions for the developers undertaking
it. Renewing subscriptions restores Development permissions for the assigned
developers for the renewed term.

5. Source distribution and retained copies
------------------------------------------

You may copy, publish, and distribute the Software in source form, including
your modifications, provided you include this License and preserve its
conditions. Source distribution does not grant access to the
BenjaVision-Catalyst repository or exempt recipients from developer
subscriptions when they undertake Development.

You may retain source copies and backups after subscription expiry. Retaining
a copy does not authorise further Development without an active subscription.
Neither distribution nor sublicensing may grant broader rights to the
Software than this License grants. In particular, recipients cannot receive
subscription-free Development rights through a distributor or a modified
version of Catalyst.

